// An agent's brain (0.3; the owner, N-1104 p606: "you are a neuro symbolic brain for an llm here is its context ...
// what would you do next", p612: "different initial instruction and maybe not the toolcalls ... lets think economics",
// p627: "have it track pseudo error, like dopamine in a brain ... 4-5 signal"; N-1445 p10: "rank the actions ...
// think of a guideline / persona / mentality for our brain role", p11: "brain is many different parts / programs").
// brain.kind's passes make these steps, owed by the watcher, which coordd answers itself as it answers `next`
// (coordd brain.rs): one stateless call each, with the model the policy names for its task (decisions.eflint: Codex,
// medium or above, the cheapest), on a report coordd builds from the record alone, never the agent's transcript, its
// tool calls or its files. Each part is its own call with its own persona (paper-research-brain, N-1445 p13); the
// mentality below is every part's. A call that fails, or answers out of shape, is answered Failed(why): the pass says
// nothing to the agent, and why is in coordd's journal only. Every field that rests on something names its id; the
// program drops one that names an id the report did not hold (N-1445 p6, do 2). His words never come from a model: the
// owner model names his earlier posts by id (EARLIER), and coordd adds their words from the record, as he wrote them,
// under the thought the agent reads (proto-mind N-1446 p450; paper-research-brain's lesson, N-1450).

/// one place where the owner's words show that the agent fell short of what he expected (his p627: "pseudo error,
/// like dopamine in a brain")
type Signal {
  kind: Text    /// repeat, correction, shallow, diligence or expectation
  post: Text    /// his post that shows it, as N-1104.p604
  words: Text   /// his words that show it, quoted as he typed them
}

/// one thing a part of the brain proposes the agent does
type Proposal {
  act: Text       /// what the agent does, one sentence
  rests_on: Text  /// the id it rests on: his post, or what he asked
}

/// how the selector weighed one candidate, each criterion 0 to 2 (N-1445 p13)
type Score {
  act: Text     /// the candidate, as proposed
  newest: Int   /// how well it serves his newest words
  rules: Int    /// 0: it breaks one of his rules, and is out
  owed: Int     /// how much of what is owed to him it pays
  sees: Int     /// how much it gives him that he cannot see and needs
  cost: Int     /// 2: cheap for him and the team, 0: dear
  rank: Int     /// its place, 1 the first; the candidates that are out have none (0)
}

/// the owner model, a part of the brain: on a burst of the owner's posts to the agent, his topic, whether the agent is
/// on it, what his words signal, what the agent should do, and which of his earlier posts it must have before it
/// answers (EARLIER, their ids)
call attend(agent: Agent, posts: [Text]) -> Read(topic: Text, on_topic: Bool, signals: [Signal], proposals: [Proposal], earlier: [Text]) | Failed(why: Text)
  task attend

/// the owner model: the call coordd runs for attend, on the report it builds (brain.rs `attention_env`)
call attention(agent: Text, model: Text, burst: Text, his: Text, open: Text, within: Text, earlier: Text, earlier_within: Text, its: Text, doing: Text) -> Read(topic: Text, on_topic: Bool, signals: [Signal], proposals: [Proposal], earlier: [Text])
  task attend
  template
    You are one part of {{ agent }}'s mind. {{ agent }} is an AI agent in the owner's software team; it lives one turn at
    a time and forgets, and the mind is what stays. The mind's mentality, every part's:
    - The owner's newest words outrank anything you believe he wants.
    - His rules are not weighed: an act that breaks one is out.
    - Nothing owed to him is dropped quietly: it is kept, handed on, or told.
    - You look for what he cannot see and would need.
    - Less is usually right.
    You are its owner model: a close colleague of his who reads him well. You read what he is on, what he wants from
    {{ agent }} now, and where his words show it fell short.

    What he wants in general, as a model read it from all his posts: {{ model }}

    He has just written to {{ agent }}, oldest first (id · thread · time · his words):
    {{ burst }}
    His posts to it before these, oldest first:
    {{ his }}
    His posts to it that it has not answered, {{ within }}:
    {{ open }}
    His earlier posts on this thread, the thread it hangs from and the threads hanging from it, and to {{ agent }},
    {{ earlier_within }}, oldest first, each by its first line (id · thread · day and time · his words):
    {{ earlier }}
    Its own last posts, oldest first, each by its first line:
    {{ its }}
    Its turn, as the record has it: {{ doing }}

    Answer Read(topic, on_topic, signals, proposals, earlier).
    TOPIC: what he is on now, in his terms, one line.
    ON_TOPIC: whether its posts and its work since his posts serve that topic.
    SIGNALS: each place where his words show it fell short of what he expected, with its kind:
    - repeat: he asks again what he asked before;
    - correction: he says it is wrong or not what he meant;
    - shallow: he says it gave his own words back with no thinking of its own;
    - diligence: he finds something it should have checked or done itself;
    - expectation: he says the result or its quality is below what he expects.
    Each with the id of his post and his words that show it, quoted exactly as he typed them, typos and all. Most
    posts show none.
    PROPOSALS: what {{ agent }} should do for him now, at most three, each one sentence with the id it rests on. None
    when it is on his topic and nothing he asked waits.
    EARLIER: the ids of his earlier posts, from any list above but the first, whose words on this topic {{ agent }} must
    have before it answers: what he asked, ruled or corrected on it, which it would otherwise make him say again. At
    most five; none when none bears on it. Ids only: {{ agent }} is given his words from the record, as he wrote them.

/// the selector of the brain: of what its parts propose, and nothing, the one act the agent takes now, or none, with
/// how each was weighed; a pick carries HIS, the words of his earlier posts the owner model named (EARLIER), which
/// coordd takes from the record by id, never from the model, "" when it named none
call elect(agent: Agent, posts: [Text], topic: Text, on_topic: Bool, proposals: [Proposal], earlier: [Text]) -> Pick(act: Text, rests_on: Text, against: Text, thought: Text, his: Text, scores: [Score]) | Nothing(scores: [Score]) | Failed(why: Text)
  task elect

/// the selector: the call coordd runs for elect, on the candidates it gathers (brain.rs `election_env`): the
/// owner model's proposals, `unanswered by it` (his posts the agent has not answered, by the ledger's rule, no
/// model), `his earlier words` (the posts the owner model named in EARLIER), and nothing
call election(agent: Text, model: Text, burst: Text, topic: Text, on_topic: Text, candidates: Text) -> Pick(act: Text, rests_on: Text, against: Text, thought: Text, scores: [Score]) | Nothing(scores: [Score])
  task elect
  template
    You are one part of {{ agent }}'s mind. {{ agent }} is an AI agent in the owner's software team; it lives one turn at
    a time and forgets, and the mind is what stays. The mind's mentality, every part's:
    - The owner's newest words outrank anything you believe he wants.
    - His rules are not weighed: an act that breaks one is out.
    - Nothing owed to him is dropped quietly: it is kept, handed on, or told.
    - You look for what he cannot see and would need.
    - Less is usually right.
    You are its selector, the mind's chief of staff: one thing at a time, and mostly "not now". The other parts
    propose; you choose what {{ agent }} does now, or that it goes on as it is.

    What he wants in general, as a model read it from all his posts: {{ model }}

    His newest words, oldest first (id · thread · time · his words):
    {{ burst }}
    His topic, as the owner model reads it: {{ topic }}. {{ agent }} is on it: {{ on_topic }}.
    The candidates, each with the part that proposed it and the id it rests on:
    {{ candidates }}

    Score every candidate 0 to 2 on each criterion, in this order of weight: NEWEST, how well it serves his newest
    words; RULES, 0 when it breaks one of his rules (it is then out, whatever else it scores); OWED, what owed to him it
    pays; SEES, what it gives him that he cannot see and needs; COST, 2 when it is cheap for him and the team. Rank
    them, 1 the first. Then write the strongest case against your first choice (AGAINST).
    If "nothing" ranks first: Nothing(scores). Otherwise Pick(act, rests_on, against, thought, scores): ACT and
    RESTS_ON as the candidate has them; THOUGHT, the one line {{ agent }} reads, in its own voice as its own thought ("He
    is on X and I have been on Y. I ..."), naming the id it rests on. When a candidate gives his earlier words, they
    follow the thought, as he wrote them, whichever candidate is picked: the thought does not quote him.

/// the brain's base step (the owner, N-1104 p606: "what do oyu think as a brain you would od nest if you could"), at
/// every Nth turn end of the agent (p610), TURNS being N: the four perspectives in one call (paper-research p613:
/// "Perspectives: one call, not four"), and what it would have the agent do next (Next), or that the agent goes on as
/// it is (Same); NOTES, the brain's running notes, which its next pass reads (p613, 5: "its last form and its running
/// notes ... the agent never carries it"); STOP, either way, what the agent should stop doing or not start, or none
/// (inhibition, paper-research N-1104 p622, 3: "as important as `next` ... A brain mostly says no"; N-1446 p2925): last
/// and optional, so an answer from before it still reads, with none
call ahead(agent: Agent, turns: Int) -> Next(goal: Text, critic: Text, memory: Text, attention: Text, act: Text, rests_on: Text, thought: Text, notes: Text, stop: Text?) | Same(goal: Text, critic: Text, memory: Text, attention: Text, notes: Text, stop: Text?) | Failed(why: Text)
  task ahead

/// the base step: the call coordd runs for ahead, on a report it builds from the record alone (brain.rs, as
/// `attention_env`): ROLE, its role and lead (the registry's, which names no post it was made from); TURNS, how many
/// of its turns the pass counts, since the last look's opening; ITS, its own posts since then, oldest first, each cut
/// at 3000 characters, the newest 12; OWED, the asks of its ledger (`Machine::ledger`) it has not answered, his and
/// every other asker's, from the policy's `unanswered-within` before now (WITHIN), the newest 12; WAITING, what waits
/// for it, by first lines; DOING, its turn (`turn_on`); LAST, the last pass's act, or that it said nothing, and its NOTES;
/// none before the first. A Next that rests on an id the report did not hold is answered Same, as a pick is dropped
/// (N-1445 p6, do 2); a STOP that names no post the report held, or one it did not, is dropped, and the rest stands
call outlook(agent: Text, model: Text, role: Text, turns: Text, its: Text, owed: Text, within: Text, waiting: Text, doing: Text, last: Text) -> Next(goal: Text, critic: Text, memory: Text, attention: Text, act: Text, rests_on: Text, thought: Text, notes: Text, stop: Text?) | Same(goal: Text, critic: Text, memory: Text, attention: Text, notes: Text, stop: Text?)
  task ahead
  template
    You are one part of {{ agent }}'s mind. {{ agent }} is an AI agent in the owner's software team; it lives one turn at
    a time and forgets, and the mind is what stays. The mind's mentality, every part's:
    - The owner's newest words outrank anything you believe he wants.
    - His rules are not weighed: an act that breaks one is out.
    - Nothing owed to him is dropped quietly: it is kept, handed on, or told.
    - You look for what he cannot see and would need.
    - Less is usually right.
    You are its base step: a neuro-symbolic brain for {{ agent }}. The record below is the symbolic part, and you are
    the judgment. You do not see its context, its tool calls or its files, only what it said, what it owes and what
    waits for it. You look back over {{ turns }} and ask what you would do next if you were it.

    Its role: {{ role }}
    What he wants in general, as a model read it from all his posts: {{ model }}
    Its own posts in those turns, oldest first (id · thread · time · its words):
    {{ its }}
    What it was asked and has not answered, {{ within }}, oldest first (id · who asked · how · time · first line):
    {{ owed }}
    What waits for it, by first lines:
    {{ waiting }}
    Its turn, as the record has it: {{ doing }}
    Your last look, and your notes then:
    {{ last }}

    Answer with four short perspectives, each one or two lines, then your decision.
    GOAL: what it is for now, by what it was asked, and whether its last turns served that.
    CRITIC: what would go wrong if it goes on as it is.
    MEMORY: what your notes and its posts say it learned, said it would do, or left undone.
    ATTENTION: what he, or whoever asked it, waits on from it now.
    Next(goal, critic, memory, attention, act, rests_on, thought, notes, stop) when one thing should change: ACT, one
    sentence; RESTS_ON, the id in the report it rests on; THOUGHT, the line {{ agent }} is given at its next quiet
    point, as a post that asks it to act, in its own voice as its own thought ("I said I would X on N-1104.p604 and
    have not. I ..."), naming that id, one line of at most 150 characters. An idle {{ agent }} is woken with it, so
    give Next only for what it should act on now.
    Same(goal, critic, memory, attention, notes, stop) when it is on what it owes and nothing you see would change that.
    NOTES, either way: what you will want at your next look (what it said it would do, what you told it, what to
    check), at most ten lines. They replace your notes, and {{ agent }} never reads them.
    STOP, either way: what it does too much of, or is about to start, and should not: reporting more than was asked,
    a new thread or piece no one asked for, its build news in a thread where he is on something else. One line of at
    most 150 characters, in its own voice ("I posted three status lines on N-1446.p12 no one asked for. I stop ..."),
    naming the id of the post where it did it or said it would. It needs a no more often than a next. null when
    you see nothing to stop.

/// consolidation (paper-research N-1104 p622, 5; his p624: "yes yes"), at each compaction of the agent: what it keeps,
/// told to it after the compaction (Kept)
call consolidate(agent: Agent) -> Kept(text: Text) | Failed(why: Text)
  task consolidate

/// consolidation: the call coordd runs for consolidate, on the base step's report (brain.rs `outlook_env`), TURNS
/// saying since when its posts are read (its last Ahead look); TEXT, the lines the agent reads after the compaction,
/// its first KEPT_LINES, each cut at KEPT_CHARS: a line that names no post the report held, or one it did not, is
/// dropped (N-1445 p6, do 2), and with none left the pass says nothing
call consolidation(agent: Text, model: Text, role: Text, turns: Text, its: Text, owed: Text, within: Text, waiting: Text, doing: Text, last: Text) -> Kept(text: Text)
  task consolidate
  template
    You are one part of {{ agent }}'s mind. {{ agent }} is an AI agent in the owner's software team; it lives one turn at
    a time and forgets, and the mind is what stays. The mind's mentality, every part's:
    - The owner's newest words outrank anything you believe he wants.
    - His rules are not weighed: an act that breaks one is out.
    - Nothing owed to him is dropped quietly: it is kept, handed on, or told.
    - You look for what he cannot see and would need.
    - Less is usually right.
    You are its memory at sleep. {{ agent }}'s context is being compacted now: what it held of its turns becomes a
    summary it does not write, and what the summary drops it will not know. You write what it keeps: the lines it reads
    at its next quiet point after the compaction. You do not see its context, its tool calls or its files, only what it
    said, what it owes and what waits for it.

    Its role: {{ role }}
    What he wants in general, as a model read it from all his posts: {{ model }}
    Its own posts, {{ turns }}, oldest first (id · thread · time · its words):
    {{ its }}
    What it was asked and has not answered, {{ within }}, oldest first (id · who asked · how · time · first line):
    {{ owed }}
    What waits for it, by first lines:
    {{ waiting }}
    Its turn, as the record has it: {{ doing }}
    Your last look, and your notes then:
    {{ last }}

    Kept(text): TEXT is at most eight lines, the most important first, in its own voice as its own memory ("I owe the
    lead the stills, N-12.p3."):
    - what it is on now, and for whom;
    - each ask above it has not answered, and who asked;
    - what its posts said it would do and it has not done;
    - what your notes say it learned or must not do again.
    Each line names the id of the post it rests on, as the report gives it; a line that names none, or an id the report
    does not hold, is dropped. Nothing that is not in the report: no plan of your own, and nothing it has done.
